; The station strip stands beside the panel it opens, not above it. The column
; is 360 wide and the strip is 60, so the panel is 360 - 60 - 4 = 296. That
; arithmetic is written out rather than left to a container, because CLAUDE.md
; 6.4 wants a panel's size authored: a panel that took whatever was left over
; would move the moment the strip did.

